    <section class="cv-block" id="legit" aria-labelledby="legit-title">
      <h2 id="legit-title">Are Udemy CompTIA exam vouchers legitimate?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — with one important distinction. Udemy is the <strong>seller of the voucher</strong>, not the exam
        provider. CompTIA owns the certification and issues it; Pearson VUE delivers and proctors the exam. That is
        why the code is redeemed in the CompTIA → Pearson VUE scheduling flow, not inside Udemy.
      </p>
      <ul class="cv-check">
        <li><strong>Who sells it:</strong> Udemy, on udemy.com. The receipt and code come from Udemy.</li>
        <li><strong>Who delivers the exam:</strong> Pearson VUE (test centre or online proctored). You schedule and reschedule there.</li>
        <li><strong>Who issues the certification:</strong> CompTIA. Udemy cannot issue, renew or verify a CompTIA certification.</li>
        <li><strong>How to verify your code:</strong> it appears in My learning → Certifications and is accepted at Pearson VUE checkout.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="cv-note">
        Red flags: a seller asking for bank transfer or crypto, codes sent by direct message, or prices far below the
        CompTIA price. Vouchers are non-transferable, so a code from a stranger may not work. Buy from the official
        Udemy voucher pages or the CompTIA store.
      </p>
    </section>

