        absolute saving varies. Judge the voucher against the CompTIA price for <em>your</em> country, not against a
        US list price.
      </p>
      <h3>When the Udemy voucher makes sense</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want one checkout for prep course and voucher, and the live voucher price beats the CompTIA price in your region.</li>
        <li>You want the retake option bundled at purchase where it is offered.</li>
        <li>You're not ready to schedule immediately but want to lock the voucher in (≥9 months validity).</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>When buying from the CompTIA store is better</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The Udemy price in your region matches or exceeds the CompTIA price.</li>
        <li>You'd rather have 12 months to schedule — the CompTIA store voucher lasts longer.</li>
        <li>You need maximum flexibility on scheduling and local-currency pricing.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Either way, remember the renewal part</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Most CompTIA certifications renew every three years via Continuing Education — no repeat exam required for most certs.</li>
        <li>The A+ requires two vouchers (Core 1 and Core 2) — budget accordingly before buying.</li>
